'''Anne Patricia Carson''' (born June 21, 1950)<ref name="Morra-2014">{{Cite web |last=Morra |first=Linda |date=September 8, 2014 |title=Anne Carson |url=https://www.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/anne-carson |access-date=May 21, 2023 |website=[[The Canadian Encyclopedia]] |archive-date=May 12, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230512193058/http://www.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/anne-carson |url-status=live }}</ref> is a Canadian academic and author. Born in Toronto, she graduated from the [[University of Toronto]] and became a professor and lecturer at several universities since 1979. Throughout her career she has taught [[classics]], [[comparative literature]], and [[creative writing]]. She has taught at the [[University of Calgary]], [[Princeton University]], [[Emory University]], [[McGill University]], [[University of Michigan]], and [[New York University]]. Carson has written more than twenty books, including collections of essays and poetry, as well as translations of ancient [[Greek tragedy|Greek tragedies]].

She has been awarded [[Guggenheim Fellowship|Guggenheim]] and [[MacArthur Fellowship]]s, has won the [[Lannan Literary Award]], two [[Griffin Poetry Prize]]s, the [[T. S. Eliot Prize]], the [[Princess of Asturias Awards|Princess of Asturias Award]], the [[Governor General's Award for English-language poetry]], and the [[PEN/Nabokov Award]], and was appointed a Member of the [[Order of Canada]] in 2005 for her contribution to Canadian letters.<ref name="Youngs-2026">{{Cite web |date=October 8, 2026 |title='Bold and inventive' Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq4g1j54nepyo |access-date=October 8, 2026 |website=[[BBC News Online|BBC News]] |language= |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261008113231/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq4g1j54nepyo |archive-date=October 8, 2026 |url-status=live|last=Youngs|first=Ian}}</ref> [[2026 Nobel Prize in Literature|In 2026]], she was awarded the [[Nobel Prize in Literature]].<ref name="NobelPrize.org">{{Cite web |title=Nobel Prize in Literature 2026 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2026/press-release/ |access-date=October 8, 2026 |publisher=[[Nobel Foundation]] |website=NobelPrize.org |language=en-US}}</ref>

